.TH _CYAML_SET_TYPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
_cyaml_set_typed \- path-write back-end (prefer cyaml_set macro)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cyaml.h>

ccol_retval_t _cyaml_set_typed(cyaml root, const char *path,
                               cyaml_node_type_t type, void *raw,
                               size_t raw_size, bool is_signed,
                               bool raw_is_char_array);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Write a scalar value to the leaf addressed by path.  For a dictionary
leaf, the key is created if absent (its immediate parent dictionary
must already exist).  For a list leaf ("#N"), the index must already
be in range; a list has no way to be auto-extended to fit an
arbitrary index, so a syntactically valid but out-of-range one fails
with ccol_key_not_found, and malformed "#N" syntax fails with
ccol_invalid_args.  Resolving the parent path (every component before
the leaf) applies the identical distinction at each intermediate
component: a missing dictionary key, or a syntactically valid but
out-of-range list index, fails with ccol_key_not_found; a non-container
(wrong-type) node or malformed "#N" syntax fails with
ccol_invalid_args.  Either way, if the leaf already exists its type is
replaced unconditionally; any composite (list, dictionary) resources
it previously held are deep-freed.

type must be one of CYAML_NULL, CYAML_BOOL, CYAML_INTEGER,
CYAML_FLOAT, or CYAML_STRING; any other value (including CYAML_LIST /
CYAML_DICTIONARY, or the internal sentinel cyaml_set's own _Generic
dispatch produces for a C type outside its accepted-type list) is
rejected with ccol_invalid_args before the target node is touched.

raw is a void pointer to the C value; raw_size is sizeof the original
C expression.  For string values, raw points to a const char * variable
unless raw_is_char_array is true, in which case raw points directly at
the char[] bytes of a string literal.

Escape sequences in path components:
  \e.   -> literal '.' in the key (not a path separator)
  \e\e   -> literal '\e' in the key
A '\e' before any other character is left unchanged.

The cyaml_set() macro is the preferred public interface and fills in
type, raw_size, is_signed, and raw_is_char_array automatically from the
compile-time type of the value expression.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
root             Root of the DOM tree.
path             Dot-separated path string.
type             YAML type of the new value.
raw              Pointer to the raw C value.
raw_size         sizeof() of the original C expression.
is_signed        Whether the integer source type is signed.
raw_is_char_array  true when raw points directly at a char[] array.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - value written.
ccol_invalid_args      - root or path is NULL, path is empty, a
                         non-container (wrong-type) node encountered
                         before the leaf, malformed '#N' index
                         syntax, or an empty component (nothing
                         between two dots, or a leading or trailing
                         dot); at any position in the path, not just
                         the leaf.
ccol_key_not_found     - a list index (leaf or intermediate) is
                         syntactically well-formed but out of range, or
                         an intermediate dictionary key needed to
                         resolve the parent path is absent (a missing
                         dictionary key at the leaf itself is not an
                         error: it is created).
ccol_not_enough_memory - internal allocation failed.
ccol_container_full    - creating a new leaf dictionary key would
                         exceed the parent's maximum representable
                         element count (not reachable in practice).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_set (macro) (3),
.BR _cyaml_get (3)
